    {
      "name": "Instructions",
      "column_widths": {"A": 110},
      "rows": [
        [{"value": "How to use this model", "bold": true, "font_size": 13}],
        [{"value": "1. Edit ONLY the yellow input cells on the 'ROI Model' sheet. Everything else recalculates automatically."}],
        [{"value": "2. Save a copy per opportunity; never overwrite the template. File name: roi-<process-name>.xlsx"}],
        [{"value": "3. Fill the matching Business Case Canvas with the summary figures (hours, FTE, savings, payback)."}],
        [{"value": ""}],
        [{"value": "Conventions", "bold": true, "font_size": 13}],
        [{"value": "- 1 FTE = 2,080 h/yr (52 weeks × 40 h)."}],
        [{"value": "- Fully loaded employee cost = $36,000/yr ($3,000/mo × 12). Hourly rate derives automatically ($36,000/2,080 ≈ $17.31/h)."}],
        [{"value": "- Both are org standards; adjust in the inputs if payroll reality differs, and say so in the business case."}],
        [{"value": ""}],
        [{"value": "Method notes", "bold": true, "font_size": 13}],
        [{"value": "- Baseline must be captured BEFORE deployment. No baseline = no credible ROI claim (org AI-strategy standard)."}],
        [{"value": "- Measure OUTCOMES (hours saved, cycle time, error rate, cost per transaction), not activity (logins, messages)."}],
        [{"value": "- Year-1 ramp factor assumes benefits grow linearly from 0 to steady state over 'Months to full adoption'. At 6 months → 75% of steady-state benefit in year 1."}],
        [{"value": "- Be conservative: use 30–60% efficiency gain and 70–85% adoption for first estimates; revisit with real data after go-live."}],
        [{"value": ""}],
        [{"value": "Hard vs soft benefits", "bold": true, "font_size": 13}],
        [{"value": "- HARD (count in the model): hours freed (at hourly rate), error/penalty reduction, materials, avoided hires."}],
        [{"value": "- SOFT (state qualitatively in the business case, do not inflate the model): employee satisfaction, compliance posture, speed/quality improvements, capacity for higher-value work."}],
        [{"value": ""}],
        [{"value": "Review cadence", "bold": true, "font_size": 13}],
        [{"value": "- Re-validate benefits quarterly after go-live (Phase 5 of the EPO playbook). Update actuals; unachieved benefits get reviewed, not hidden."}],
        [{"value": "- If payback > 3 years or net benefit ≤ 0, challenge the case before funding."}]
      ]
    }
  ]
